I have traced the complete flow. Here is the full report.

# POST /api/owners — Complete Request-Handling Path

The endpoint is served by the **V1 controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`), which implements the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface. The V2 controller does **not** define `addOwner`. There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`), no entity listeners, and no Hibernate Envers auditing anywhere in `src/` — "auditing" here is only an SLF4J log line.

---

## 1. The mapping / route (generated interface)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`, lines 79-87:

```java
@RequestMapping(
    method = RequestMethod.POST,
    value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,          // "/owners"
    produces = { "application/json" },
    consumes = { "application/json" }
)
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... }
```

Key point: the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` triggers Bean Validation **before** the controller body runs. The controller class base path is `/api` (`@RequestMapping("/api")`), so the full path is `POST /api/owners`.

---

## 2. The @RestController method

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration (lines 60-63):
```java
@RestController
@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")
@RequestMapping("/api")
public class OwnerRestControllerV1 implements OwnersApi {
```

The handler (lines 110-136):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);                     // (A) mapping — runs normalizers/validators
    Collection<Owner> owners = this.clinicService.findAllOwners();          // (B) load all owners
    if (DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached(owners)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);         // 429
    }
    if (IdentityKey.isDuplicate(owners, owner)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);                  // 409
    }
    if (CityCapacity.isFull(owners, owner)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);                  // 409
    }
    owner.setNamesakeCount(NamesakeCounter.count(owners, owner));
    owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCodeGenerator.generate(owners, owner));
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignupWarning.isTriggered(owners));
    owner.setHouseholdSize((int) owners.stream().filter(o -> HouseholdMatcher.sameHousehold(o, owner)).count() + 1);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);                                    // (C) persist
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);                      // (D) map to response, computes derived fields
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);     // 201
}
```

Security: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` references the `Roles` bean (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java`), `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"`. Note this method is **not** annotated `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`), so each `clinicService` call is its own transaction.

**Ordering of checks/side-effects in the controller:** (1) map/normalize DTO → Owner; (2) load all owners; (3) daily-limit → 429; (4) duplicate identity → 409; (5) city full → 409; (6) set namesakeCount; (7) set customerCode; (8) set bulkSignupWarning; (9) set householdSize; (10) save; (11) audit log; (12) map to DTO; (13) 201 with Location header.

---

## 3. The request-body DTO with all validation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`

Bean Validation constraints (evaluated by `@Valid` at bind time, before the controller body):

- `firstName` (line 73): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 94): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 115): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*") @Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `city` (line 136): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*") @Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone` (line 157): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[+()\\d\\s-]+$") @Size(min = 1, max = 20)`
- `email` (line 178): `@Size(max = 255) @jakarta.validation.constraints.Email` (optional)
- `postcode` (line 199): `@Pattern(regexp = "^\\d{4}$")` (optional)
- `registrationDate` (line 220): `@Valid` (optional `LocalDate`)
- `sharesHousehold` (lines 232-251): no constraints (optional `Boolean`) — note this field is read from the DTO but is **not** referenced by the controller or mapper in the create path.

---

## 4. The MapStruct mapper — `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (side-effects during mapping)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`, lines 34-65:

```java
@Mapping(target = "id", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "pets", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "telephone", qualifiedByName = "normalizeTelephone")
@Mapping(target = "address", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.service.AddressNormalizer.normalize(ownerDto.getAddress()))")
@Mapping(target = "postcode", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.service.PostcodeValidator.validate(ownerDto.getCity(), ownerDto.getPostcode()))")
Owner toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerDto);

@Named("normalizeTelephone")
default String normalizeTelephone(String telephone) {
    if (telephone == null) return null;
    boolean international = telephone.trim().startsWith("+");
    String digits = telephone.replaceAll("\\D", "");
    if (!international) {
        if (digits.startsWith("0")) digits = digits.substring(1);
        digits = "61" + digits;
    }
    if (digits.length() < 8 || digits.length() > 15)
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Telephone cannot form a valid E.164 number: " + telephone);
    org.springframework.samples.petclinic.service.E164NationalLength.check(digits);
    return "+" + digits;
}
```

The generated mapper impl also auto-maps the remaining like-named fields (`firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `email`, `registrationDate`) via their setters. This matters because the **entity setters have side-effects** (see §5). Mapping-time validators that can throw `IllegalArgumentException` (→ 400 via the advice, see §7):

- **`normalizeTelephone`** — strips non-digits, assumes `+61` when no leading `+`, drops a national leading `0`, enforces 8-15 digits, then calls `E164NationalLength.check`.
- **`E164NationalLength.check`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/E164NationalLength.java`) — `+61` requires exactly 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10; else throws.
- **`AddressNormalizer.normalize`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/AddressNormalizer.java`) — trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE; throws if blank after normalization.
- **`PostcodeValidator.validate`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/PostcodeValidator.java`) — returns null if postcode absent; otherwise resolves region via `LocalityResolver.locality(city)` and throws if the 4-digit postcode is outside NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099 (UNKNOWN region accepts any).

---

## 5. The `Owner` entity — validation, defaults, and setter side-effects

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address") @NotEmpty private String address;
    @Column(name = "city")    @NotEmpty private String city;
    @Column(name = "telephone")
    @NotEmpty
    @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be E.164: '+' followed by 8 to 15 digits")
    private String telephone;
    @Column(name = "email") private String email;
    @Column(name = "postcode") private String postcode;
    @Column(name = "registration_date") private LocalDate registrationDate;
    @Transient private String customerCode;
    @Transient private Integer namesakeCount;
    @Transient private Boolean bulkSignupWarning;
    @Transient private Integer householdSize;
    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<Pet> pets;
```

Two setters with **side-effects**, invoked during MapStruct mapping in §4:

```java
/** Store the email lower-cased ... */                              // lines 104-106
public void setEmail(String email) {
    this.email = (email == null) ? null : email.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}

/** Default a missing registration date to the server's current date. */  // lines 121-123
public void setRegistrationDate(LocalDate registrationDate) {
    this.registrationDate = BusinessDay.adjust((registrationDate == null) ? LocalDate.now() : registrationDate);
}
```

So the `registrationDate` default (today) and business-day roll-forward happen **inside the entity setter during mapping**, before any of the controller's date-based checks (`DailyRegistrationLimit`, `BulkSignupWarning`) run.

`BusinessDay.adjust` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BusinessDay.java`): a Saturday/Sunday is rolled forward to the following Monday; weekdays unchanged.

Inherited fields — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`:
```java
@Column(name = "first_name") @NotEmpty protected String firstName;
@Column(name = "last_name")  @NotEmpty protected String lastName;
```
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java`:
```java
@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY) protected Integer id;
public boolean isNew() { return this.id == null; }
```

Note: the entity's `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints are only enforced if a `Validator` runs on the entity (e.g., Hibernate `pre-insert` validation via `jakarta.validation`). They are not explicitly invoked in this path; the DTO validation in §3 is what runs at bind time. The entity's `telephone @Pattern` (`^\+[0-9]{8,15}$`) matches the normalized output of `normalizeTelephone`.

---

## 6. The controller's helper checks / derived-field generators

All in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/`:

- `DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached` — true when ≥ `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` existing owners share today's (business-day-adjusted) registrationDate → 429.
- `IdentityKey.isDuplicate` — true when an existing owner matches on both telephone **and** email (email null treated as "") → 409. (`IdentityKey.of` builds `telephone|email|householdId`, used only for the response DTO.)
- `CityCapacity.isFull` — true when ≥ `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` owners already in the same city (case-insensitive) → 409.
- `NamesakeCounter.count` — count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive); stored in transient `namesakeCount`.
- `CustomerCodeGenerator.generate` — `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, sequence = (owners already in that city) + 1; stored in transient `customerCode`.
- `BulkSignupWarning.isTriggered` — true when > `THRESHOLD = 80` owners share today's registrationDate; stored in transient `bulkSignupWarning`.
- `HouseholdMatcher.sameHousehold` / `householdId` — same normalized last name + address; `householdSize` = matching existing owners + 1.

These are pure static helpers (no persistence, no events, no email).

---

## 7. Service layer + repository save

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`:

```java
@Override @Transactional(readOnly = true)                 // lines 126-129
public Collection<Owner> findAllOwners() throws DataAccessException {
    return ownerRepository.findAll();
